{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games","id":1016173,"title":"Unusual settings for games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-12T11:38:58-08:00","id":1016173,"title":"Unusual settings for games","content":"What are some unusual setting for games you've played, or settings you'd like to play in?<br /> <br /> For me, I'd like to do a game set in Antarctica, where the players are researchers who stumble across some horror. Think John Carpenter's <i>The Thing</i>.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to do a Werewolf game set in Las Vegas. The city is a testament to humanity's alienation from nature, and there could be lots of cool spirits as well (gambling spirits, lust spirits, etc.) It's also in the same desert as one of the least hospitable places in the country.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12761-suzuki","name":"Suzuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T12:57:20-08:00","id":1016207,"title":"","content":"I haven't got it off the ground yet but I'm working on a game set in space, set aboard a generational style ship making a mission to mars to establish a colony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T14:26:13-08:00","id":1016243,"title":"","content":"Weirdest setting for me was Jurassic Park. Aside from rolling science to notice that everything Jeff Goldblum's character said was wrong, it was actually a really intense survival horror scenario.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suzuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games#post1016173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, I'd like to do a game set in Antarctica, where the players are researchers who stumble across some horror. Think John Carpenter's <i>The Thing</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've played that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T14:28:39-08:00","id":1016246,"title":"","content":"Having watched Legends of Tomorrow recently, I've got rough plans for a Time Travelling game. Mages, Demons, Changelings, and Mummies would fit right in. All the others would also fit as &quot;misfits who have no business messing with the timeline - but are doing it anyways&quot;.<br /> <br /> Dark Eras is very useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T16:40:35-08:00","id":1016311,"title":"","content":"I want to do a game set in one of the many atlantises with it on the brink of being erased from existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T18:52:46-08:00","id":1016353,"title":"","content":"How about right after the fall, survivors in a hostile world still pinning for what they lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T00:18:54-08:00","id":1016442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games?p=1016353#post1016353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about right after the fall, survivors in a hostile world still pinning for what they lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>This shouldn't be possible, because the Fall retroactively excised the Awakened City from existence. There cannot be a time after an event that did not happen, there cannot be survivors of a disaster that never occured, and people cannot pine for the loss of what they never had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T00:40:35-08:00","id":1016447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games?p=1016442#post1016442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This shouldn't be possible, because the Fall retroactively excised the Awakened City from existence. There cannot be a time after an event that did not happen, there cannot be survivors of a disaster that never occured, and people cannot pine for the loss of what they never had.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Fomor the Recursive, Seventh Sub-Soul of Papillon the Dissonant, Aswadim and Archmaster of Time:</b> Ah, I see you've read our flier!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T00:50:43-08:00","id":1016451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games?p=1016447#post1016447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Fomor the Recursive, Seventh Sub-Soul of Papillon the Dissonant, Aswadim and Archmaster of Time:</b> Ah, I see you've read our flier!</div> </div> </div> </div>Dammit, I thought I blocked all of those spam ads - they keep getting into my mailbox!<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, can archmages go back to the Time Before?<br /> (Then again, archmages have been known to consult things like causality as useful guidelines at best, and the Scelesti have been known to laugh at anything that looks like a guideline at any level of power)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T07:14:19-08:00","id":1016534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games?p=1016442#post1016442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This shouldn't be possible, because the Fall retroactively excised the Awakened City from existence. There cannot be a time after an event that did not happen, there cannot be survivors of a disaster that never occured, and people cannot pine for the loss of what they never had.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I would presume in the discussed Setting the Fall doesn't (yet) exist. So their city/cities wouldn't have not existed at that point in relative time.<br /> <br /> My question, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a>, would be does the setting take place pre-Fall, during Fall, or post-Fall, and if it spans them, how much of each span is involved? It would be a very good 3 act setup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 12-13-2016, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T07:53:22-08:00","id":1016548,"title":"","content":"1e Mage still exists and it spent a lot of ink dealing with the Fall as a historical event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T08:06:35-08:00","id":1016553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games?p=1016451#post1016451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more serious note, can archmages go back to the Time Before?<br /> (Then again, archmages have been known to consult things like causality as useful guidelines at best, and the Scelesti have been known to laugh at anything that looks like a guideline at any level of power)</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely they can try to RECREATE Time Before - it's exactly what 8 Archmages in my private games are doing since <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2012_phenomenon\" target=\"_blank\">21 December of 2012</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Well, they even awaken from stasis slumber on last their tries to recreate <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened-mage-timeline#post387074\">Atlantis, this circa 1500 BCE.</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> One of them woken erlier and made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/718396-dark-eras-to-the-strongest-first-order-caucus\">first Eastern Caucus of Admantine Arrow</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-13-2016, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T08:29:40-08:00","id":1016568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suzuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games#post1016173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are some unusual setting for games you've played, or settings you'd like to play in?<br /> <br /> For me, I'd like to do a game set in Antarctica, where the players are researchers who stumble across some horror. Think John Carpenter's <i>The Thing</i>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in Antarctica right now. Let me tell you... if you stumble across something, it'll probably be in a thousand foot deep crevasse. But if you want to work with existing structure, look at McMurdo Station Antarctica. We're next to a volcano, and a spot were the sea ice periodically melts/beaks up.<br /> <br /> As to what I'd run: WtF 2e. A Forsaken in NASA noticed a foreign body approaching the earth. None of his coworkers seem to be able to see it. A protectorate is about to send a number of wolves to become astronauts, and find out what this is. The Body is an alien space station, a prison formed to hold an Idagram. The inhabitants have been corrupted, and the Idagram has nearly unlocked itself. What will our forsaken (space) wolves do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T08:40:33-08:00","id":1016576,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I wonder how much mileage you could get out of a traditional &quot;dungeon crawl&quot;, but in the context of: someone found a backdoor into the Primordial Dream. You and your team are invested/conscripted/contracted into delving the &quot;depths&quot; of vacant and not-so-vacant Chambers in search of knowledge and treasure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T13:14:08-08:00","id":1016700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games?p=1016534#post1016534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a>, would be does the setting take place pre-Fall, during Fall, or post-Fall, and if it spans them, how much of each span is involved? It would be a very good 3 act setup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Post-fall, especially since there might never have been a fall to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T15:19:57-08:00","id":1016769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games?p=1016243#post1016243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've played that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>How did it go?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games?p=1016568#post1016568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm in Antarctica right now. Let me tell you... if you stumble across something, it'll probably be in a thousand foot deep crevasse. But if you want to work with existing structure, look at McMurdo Station Antarctica. We're next to a volcano, and a spot were the sea ice periodically melts/beaks up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I ask what you're doing in Antarctica? It sounds cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12761-suzuki","name":"Suzuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T15:22:25-08:00","id":1016770,"title":"","content":"I ran a Mage game set in Silent Hill.<br /> <br /> I&quot;m preparing a Mage campaign set in the Mojave of Fallout New Vegas<br /> <br /> I'm writing WOD adaptations of Fall from Heaven, a mod for Civ 4, Warcraft, and Alpha Centauri<br /> <br /> While published I'm trying to encourage people around me to run a Mage Neolithic game, the Vinca setting is simply wondrous","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T15:55:25-08:00","id":1016782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suzuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games?p=1016769#post1016769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did it go?</div> </div> </div> </div>Due to an unrelated misunderstanding I turned traitor on the group and had to murder them all. Then the monster killed me which was fair enough really.<br /> <br /> The scenario was essentially The Thing if the Norwegians had dug up an Elder Thing instead. Though the GM put a lot of thought into making the Alien genuinely alien and terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T16:25:38-08:00","id":1016800,"title":"","content":"I ran a one-shot of Mummy during the Urabi Revolt in Alexandria, that was supposed to lead into a full chronicle based on that city throughout the ages. I also had a Vampire chronicle that failed right out of the gate due to pretty terrible players based in 1700s Montreal.<br /> <br /> It's tough being the only history nerd in a given circle of friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T17:12:38-08:00","id":1016819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suzuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games#post1016173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are some unusual setting for games you've played, or settings you'd like to play in?<br /> <br /> For me, I'd like to do a game set in Antarctica, where the players are researchers who stumble across some horror. Think John Carpenter's <i>The Thing</i>.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to do a Werewolf game set in Las Vegas. The city is a testament to humanity's alienation from nature, and there could be lots of cool spirits as well (gambling spirits, lust spirits, etc.) It's also in the same desert as one of the least hospitable places in the country.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a born and raised Vegas boy, I'd agree that we'd have one weird Shadow. I'd imagine the Strip as this island. A mighty fortress of neon and steel, hoarding all the ambient essence directed at Vegas from afar, ruled over by Jackpot and Lady Luck. Around the strip is a brief warzone of slums, homeless tent villages, shoals, fear, death, and sadness. Then, just past that, its a normal town, if a little sad and desperate, with a few more exciting and liberal spirits. <br /> <br /> Of course, there is the rumor that some massive, sleeping evil deep underneath the Vegas valley. Who knows what that could be. And of course, the water spirits in the whole area are manmade and domesticated by the casino and resort gods. Still, Redrock canyon would be a great place for some iron masters (who may look coyoteish) to set up and make progress through the suburbs towards the Ivory Claw supported Strip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T17:23:27-08:00","id":1016827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games?p=1016819#post1016819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a born and raised Vegas boy, I'd agree that we'd have one weird Shadow. I'd imagine the Strip as this island. A mighty fortress of neon and steel, hoarding all the ambient essence directed at Vegas from afar, ruled over by Jackpot and Lady Luck. Around the strip is a brief warzone of slums, homeless tent villages, shoals, fear, death, and sadness. Then, just past that, its a normal town, if a little sad and desperate, with a few more exciting and liberal spirits. <br /> <br /> Of course, there is the rumor that some massive, sleeping evil deep underneath the Vegas valley. Who knows what that could be. And of course, the water spirits in the whole area are manmade and domesticated by the casino and resort gods. Still, Redrock canyon would be a great place for some iron masters (who may look coyoteish) to set up and make progress through the suburbs towards the Ivory Claw supported Strip.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take a gander at Tim Power's Last Call and Ken Hite's mini-supplement on Vegas in 1968 if you want a jumping-off point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T22:17:14-08:00","id":1016912,"title":"","content":"I've just started a sci-fi campaign of Hunter. I wanted the players to be hunting aliens or weirdly mutant people.<br /> <br /> Here is my pitch, if you are interested:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=17f47IHxe9lJmkX5wf-usfIR_lUeQQSyKI61Tjt96Gyo\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=17f47IHxe9lJmkX5wf-usfIR_lUeQQSyKI61Tjt96Gyo\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=17f47IHxe9lJmkX5wf-usfIR_lUeQQSyKI61Tjt96Gyo\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/open?id=17f47IHxe9lJmkX5wf-usfIR_lUeQQSyKI61Tjt96Gyo </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> We've only had one session so far, and it ran a bit like Shadowrun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12767-spandexandy","name":"SpandexAndy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T22:35:12-08:00","id":1016918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpandexAndy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games?p=1016912#post1016912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've just started a sci-fi campaign of Hunter. I wanted the players to be hunting aliens or weirdly mutant people.<br /> <br /> Here is my pitch, if you are interested:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=17f47IHxe9lJmkX5wf-usfIR_lUeQQSyKI61Tjt96Gyo\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=17f47IHxe9lJmkX5wf-usfIR_lUeQQSyKI61Tjt96Gyo\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=17f47IHxe9lJmkX5wf-usfIR_lUeQQSyKI61Tjt96Gyo\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/open?id=17f47IHxe9lJmkX5wf-usfIR_lUeQQSyKI61Tjt96Gyo </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> We've only had one session so far, and it ran a bit like Shadowrun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks breddy gud to me. It looks like there aren;t any &quot;traditional&quot; CofD elements in the game (as in vampires, werewolves, etc.). Are there organizations that mirror the compacts and conspiracies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12761-suzuki","name":"Suzuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T00:28:26-08:00","id":1016930,"title":"","content":"No, you are right, I don't have traditional vampires, etc. I was hoping to use the Horrors and Dread Powers in the CofD book to make things up. I have mortal organizations with their own agents, but I intended for the PCs to be independent, and hired adhoc by these organizations for missions, but not under their authority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12767-spandexandy","name":"SpandexAndy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T07:45:37-08:00","id":1017060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suzuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games?p=1016769#post1016769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I ask what you're doing in Antarctica? It sounds cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'm just here issuing tools and waiting for something in my field of expertise (sheet metal) to break. One the whole, we (the military) support the scientific operations that the National Science Foundation wants to run, including climate science projects, biology/ecology projects, and terrain mapping. Mostly that means we ferry them and their supplies around the continent via aircraft.<br /> <br /> Edit: On topic, I'd also like to do something based in a less Urban area- somewhere very middle of nowhere, with a wild west feel to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","user":"ArchonAres","date":". 12-14-2016, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T10:20:43-08:00","id":1017136,"title":"","content":"The first werewolf game I ran involved a long excursion to Morocco and the desert.<br /> <br /> The current mage game I'm running will jump through various Dark Eras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:08:03-08:00","id":1017158,"title":"","content":"I'm running an apocalyptic world travel game set after the Dark Mother returns to the physical world through a mortal host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T18:12:44-08:00","id":1017419,"title":"","content":"I flirted with the idea of setting a game in a Terry Brooks, Shannara sort of world. Namely a post apocalyptic world that was so post the apocalypse that a new world has arisen with the previous and its fall becoming the basis of myth and legend. Part of the setting would be the possibility of not only ancient, supernatural relics but also relics of super science like A.I., cybernetic war machines and killer satellites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T19:30:20-08:00","id":1017448,"title":"","content":"I have a great idea for a campaign based in Peshawar, Pakistan in the 80s. There's so much opportunity for dramatic skullduggery. Hundreds of agencies from around the world, thousands of refugees, arms dealers everywhere (finally an opportunity for players to actually legitimately get a bazooka), money pouring in to warlords, but lots of poverty. Peshawar was the gateway to Afghanistan in the war with the Soviets, and it would be a fantastic setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T10:45:00-08:00","id":1017712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suzuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games#post1016173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, I'd like to do a game set in Antarctica, where the players are researchers who stumble across some horror. Think John Carpenter's <i>The Thing</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check out Promethean 2E! There's a brief Antarctica writetup, and an arch-qashmal hanging out there that riffs on The Thing in an interesting way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T11:29:00-08:00","id":1017726,"title":"","content":"I think an &quot;Ice Age apocalypse&quot; Promethean chronicle could easily use the Antarctica material as inspiration: humanity has been reduced to a few isolated pockets just trying to survive from day to day, praying that whatever source of food and fuel they have doesn't run out. It would certainly put the Pilgrimage in an interesting light, because why go through all that if your just going to face extinction sooner or later? As humanity's flame begins to sputter, do Prometheans keep searching, or does it turn into one big miserable Flux fest? <br /> <br /> Stemming off of that, &quot;Wolf's Rain&quot; provides some fun inspiration for a Werewolf Ice Age chronicle: the main characters are wolves with the ability to disguise themselves as humans, living in a world where humans have guaranteed the imminent extinction of the wolf. Too bad humanity's only hope of survival rests with the very animals they've been trying to destroy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T18:36:38-08:00","id":1018287,"title":"","content":"I ran a very successful, very full campaign on a non-terraformed Mars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T20:07:33-08:00","id":1018308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games?p=1018287#post1018287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ran a very successful, very full campaign on a non-terraformed Mars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which gameline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12761-suzuki","name":"Suzuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T07:08:25-08:00","id":1018446,"title":"","content":"I can imagine a very fun game about a group of Unchained who all took over the first group of astronauts to Mars so they could create their own, personal, Hell there. This goes about as well as expected. Queue ancient God-Machine Infrastructure, million year old ruins from the things before, and other cool, pulpy things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T12:34:55-08:00","id":1018548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suzuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games?p=1018308#post1018308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which gameline?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, Geist and Changeling. Here is my elevator pitch:<br /> <br /> The first Mars colonies were established in the 2030s, and others soon followed. Mining operations on asteroids and Mars became big business and the corporate concerns that oversaw them bloated under their weight. Earth started to run out of clean water and food about ten years later. Decades of political squabbling over the truth of any potential problems left a world devoid of solutions to those problems, and riots began. The same story of ages past played out before \u2013 war burst out, colonies stopped imports and exports, and people stranded in the reaches of space began to die.<br /> <br /> The Martians didn't.<br /> <br /> They buckled down and weathered the vanishing support with fortitude and perseverance born out of their frontier ancestors and they lived \u2013 thrived, you might even say \u2013 in the cold, red wastes. Gangs became tribes, and tribes warred amongst each other over dwindling resources, renewable energy materiel, and found ways to integrate ever stranger things into their bodies, to better stave off the terrible climate. A century passed, and signals from Earth came again. The companies that put the ancestors on the red dust came back and claimed ownership over the Martians and their tools, and the Martian propensity for war turned up.<br /> <br /> That didn't work out too well; the invaders held the ultimate high ground, and even with all their cybernetics and emancipated robots and reborn machinery, the Martians did not win the day. The companies came down and reprogrammed what they could, fixed what they couldn't, extracted hefty fees from the rebels, and locked down the colonies. Now mines and work camps are little more than prisons, and they make them more like that every day, shipping in new meat from Earth to grind up in the mines looking for gold and copper, ignoring the tribes living squalid existences in the dust.<br /> <br /> The corporate concerns sit in orbit in their glittering homes with terraforming implements and gases all sitting and waiting for the button to be pressed to turn Mars into a new Earth, but they don't because the bottom line says that would lose them more money than it would save. They set lights out and exercise periods and uniform requirements for employees on the ground and implement their decisions through ruthless robotic stand-ins. It's 2150 and it's same-shit, different-day.<br /> <br /> Maybe you died. You suffocated in the thin air, you got pulped by a mining machine, you were the last survivor of a Martian raid or a casualty of war. Whatever happened, you got back up, you just had something else in your brain that tells you to kill, to fight back, to let the Martian dead find their rest and their exaltation in war.<br /> <br /> Maybe you went somewhere you shouldn't have. You found yourself in a winding canyon during exploratory EVA, your ship crashed someplace it couldn't have, your adulthood ritual among the tribe went wrong, and you found yourself in some other Mars, someplace with canals and angry red weeds and Martian cabbage and you took water with strange booming things in the depths of the caverns or hiding amongst the sharp-edged ruins and you know <i>that </i>Mars is still out there, and it wants to be let out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T11:21:53-08:00","id":1019869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games?p=1016207#post1016207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't got it off the ground yet but I'm working on a game set in space, set aboard a generational style ship making a mission to mars to establish a colony.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I love this. I love Mars. Anything Mars related. Awesome. <br /> <br /> 2. I'm pretty sure that at max, a ship only takes about 9-10 months to get to Mars (and around 3-4 if the new EM drive pans out as planned). Either way i'm not sure it's enough time for a generation to pass. Hardly enough time for a full pregnancy period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T12:05:41-08:00","id":1019892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games?p=1019869#post1019869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I love this. I love Mars. Anything Mars related. Awesome.<br /> <br /> 2. I'm pretty sure that at max, a ship only takes about 9-10 months to get to Mars (and around 3-4 if the new EM drive pans out as planned). Either way i'm not sure it's enough time for a generation to pass. Hardly enough time for a full pregnancy period.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they meant in the style of generation ships - IE, having everything on it necessary to supporting life. Which, if it is good enough for the ship, means it is most likely good enough to support the colonists on the surface as well. Helps to be able to sustain those colonists, after all.<br /> <br /> Though that does bring up the other scenario: Mars was &quot;pre-colonized&quot; by robots to make it ready for human (and non) colonists. But what will the colonists find when they actually arrive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T12:36:33-08:00","id":1019916,"title":"","content":"I've got a few ideas for more human and human+ settings.<br /> <br /> One is a faux fantasy world... that was formed by a Ring of Unchained suborning enough Infrastructure to split off part of the earth and set themselves up as gods. Gods are Unchained. Heroes (in the Greek sense) are Offspring and Fractals. Sorcerers are Stigmatics. &quot;Magic&quot; items are Gadgets. Monsters are Cryptids. Weird religious ceremonies and prophetic convergences are Occult Matrices. Anachronistic tech abounds. Targeted for a different, grittier (due to the CofD ruleset) take on High Fantasy.<br /> <br /> Another is based on Leviathan, inspired by the Cinder Spires and Dishonored. It's an &quot;After the End&quot; world on the slow road to recovery. Technology used to be higher, but is now poorly understood and rediscovered. The Marduk Society is a full on society, largely keeping themselves as high up and away from the water as possible. Less developed people are reduced to Bronze Age near-barabarism and often worship the Deep Ones (Leviathans). The Leviathans themselves war amongst each other in the seas, using their mutant (Hybrid) cultists as proxies. Oh, and in the undefined frontier, a cabal of Atolls is enslaving Leviathans as their personal monsters. Targeted for Conan-esque adventure, lite eldritch horror, and ruthless pragmatism.<br /> <br /> Another one I just thought up is a Judge Dredd-like survivor setting with Werewolf. Humanity and Spirits are crowded into some mega-city structure and forced to work together. Werewolves have to keep the peace and the balance between them. Basically an overt rehash of the &quot;Spirit Cops&quot; concept, but more Cop. And they are out in the open. But answerable to superiors (who may well be human). [This one isn't Human+, though]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T16:18:26-08:00","id":1020038,"title":"","content":"My players and I came up with a system of rolling die to determine the core book used, theme, and setting for one shot games we play occasionally around our main game. I'm currently waiting for Bollywood or Soap Opera to come up as the theme. We've currently got a Changeling road trip in space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12771-revanreborn","name":"RevanReborn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12771_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T16:50:59-08:00","id":1020058,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar654_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"654\" data-vbnamecard=\"654\">xiongrey</a> it is like vent0 is saying, I call it a generational ship because it'd be capable of supporting generations if nessisary while settlements are established. <br /> <br /> To further expand on the idea, in this game the god machine only exists on earth. This whole mission is the god machine testing if it can spread beyond earth. A worry that if humans destroy earth and themselves it could either join them or greatly have its efficiency reduced. <br /> <br /> Of course the party wouldn't know this going in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T07:05:25-08:00","id":1020371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games?p=1020058#post1020058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar654_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"654\" data-vbnamecard=\"654\">xiongrey</a> it is like vent0 is saying, I call it a generational ship because it'd be capable of supporting generations if nessisary while settlements are established.<br /> <br /> To further expand on the idea, in this game the god machine only exists on earth. This whole mission is the god machine testing if it can spread beyond earth. A worry that if humans destroy earth and themselves it could either join them or greatly have its efficiency reduced.<br /> <br /> Of course the party wouldn't know this going in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooo. Alternate plot thread: Mars was once inhabited by &quot;people&quot; and the Earth-God-Machine's predecessor (or a parallel, localised splinter, if the G-M transcends one mere planet). What happens when it uncovers just what happens when it doesn't play nice with Its toys? What about any Unchained analogs that might still hibernate beneath the cold red sands?<br /> <hr /><br /> Really, any particular instance of Mars being previously inhabited would work with most of the splats.<br /> <br /> Werewolf - Where the <s>Wild Things</s> Idigam Are<br /> Promethean - Finding out the surface/Olympus Mons/ underground is <i>filled</i> with Pandorans<br /> Changeling - Opening a Hedge-Gate and finding the locale Hedge is <i>covered</i> in Iron chains and warnings to Stay Out.<br /> Geist - Finding Mars isn't empty.<br /> <hr /><br /> More Mars idea fun:<br /> <br /> The PCs encounter a deranged Decieved claiming to be from the far future when Earth is uninhabitable, having used dangerous forbidden powers to cast themselves backwards in time.<br /> <br /> Or, the Mummy PCs Awaken to find their remains tampered with by the colonists/explorers. Turns out, their cults had enough of their crap last Descent and secreted their remains upon one of the Mars lander missions, years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 12-21-2016, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T09:41:35-08:00","id":1020446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1016173-unusual-settings-for-games?p=1020371#post1020371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oooo. Alternate plot thread: Mars was once inhabited by &quot;people&quot; and the Earth-God-Machine's predecessor (or a parallel, localised splinter, if the G-M transcends one mere planet). What happens when it uncovers just what happens when it doesn't play nice with Its toys? What about any Unchained analogs that might still hibernate beneath the cold red sands?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2909_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2909\" data-vbnamecard=\"2909\">Mr.F.I.X.</a> , gotcha makes sense, sorry for the misunderstanding ^.^.<br /> <br /> Ohhhh, to expand on the the plot thread you and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> are coming up with. What if the G-M of Earth is non-cooperational of the G-M of Mars. What if they split up eons in the past or developed separately and neither want the other there. (this would need a scaling down of the typical uber cosmological scale that the G-M is typically portrayed as). Kind of a cool setting where the players have to combat the difficulties of Mars as well as being caught in a physical/meta-physical war between two G-M entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider